  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.56,
      "end_seconds": 3.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "hello, come in mind the step"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 4.45,
      "end_seconds": 8.8,
      "duration_seconds": 4.35,
      "text": "Doctor, I'm just here to help with the details."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 9.55,
      "end_seconds": 14.38,
      "duration_seconds": 4.83,
      "text": "Absolutely, come and sit beside them. So, what's the problem?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 16.12,
      "end_seconds": 25.36,
      "duration_seconds": 9.24,
      "text": "Right, um, it's bloating after meals. I thought I'd wait, but it hasn't gone."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 27.05,
      "end_seconds": 36.28,
      "duration_seconds": 9.23,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Temp 36.4 degrees, respiratory rate 18, BP is 113 over 74, pulse is 84 beats a minute."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 37.12,
      "end_seconds": 39.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.76,
      "text": "Good, thank you. Since when exactly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 40.77,
      "end_seconds": 43.78,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "Around three weeks, I think."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 44.77,
      "end_seconds": 48.41,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "it was closer to a month, doctor"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 50.23,
      "end_seconds": 54.5,
      "duration_seconds": 4.27,
      "text": "Okay, so roughly three to four weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 56.29,
      "end_seconds": 58.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "Yeah, uh, roughly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 60.04,
      "end_seconds": 62.97,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "How troublesome is it day to day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 64.28,
      "end_seconds": 66.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "I'd call it severe."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 67.22,
      "end_seconds": 74.99,
      "duration_seconds": 7.77,
      "text": "And the other thing I wanted to to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 75.09,
      "end_seconds": 83.46,
      "duration_seconds": 8.37,
      "text": "Let me think, you know, tell the doctor about the other thing, that's what worries me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 85.07,
      "end_seconds": 102.4,
      "duration_seconds": 17.33,
      "text": "Hmm, um, I was getting to that! As for loose stools now and then, I honestly can't say when that began. It might have been last month or the month before."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 103.09,
      "end_seconds": 105.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.03,
      "text": "is anything making it worse?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 105.93,
      "end_seconds": 109.09,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "Stress definitely sets it it off."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 110.93,
      "end_seconds": 113.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "Have you had a lot of wind?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 114.57,
      "end_seconds": 116.53,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "Yeah, that too."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 124.13,
      "end_seconds": 128.14,
      "duration_seconds": 4.01,
      "text": "And blood in the stool, any of that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 129.16,
      "end_seconds": 138.37,
      "duration_seconds": 9.21,
      "text": "sorry, uh, what was I saying, no, I haven't had any blood in the stool"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.15,
      "end_seconds": 145.2,
      "duration_seconds": 6.05,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any weight loss, vomiting or night-time diarrhoea?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 150.26,
      "end_seconds": 153.36,
      "duration_seconds": 3.1,
      "text": "None of those, um, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 153.91,
      "end_seconds": 157.96,
      "duration_seconds": 4.05,
      "text": "alright, any problems with your joints or muscles?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 158.55,
      "end_seconds": 160.28,
      "duration_seconds": 1.73,
      "text": "No, nothing there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 165.24,
      "end_seconds": 169.14,
      "duration_seconds": 3.9,
      "text": "Let me ask about allergies, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 169.9,
      "end_seconds": 171.38,
      "duration_seconds": 1.48,
      "text": "no known allergies"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 176.89,
      "end_seconds": 184.34,
      "duration_seconds": 7.45,
      "text": "mm, I'm not sure that's right. I seem to recall a problem with erythromycin"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 185.47,
      "end_seconds": 188.64,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "Yeah, really? I don't think so."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 190.08,
      "end_seconds": 194.86,
      "duration_seconds": 4.78,
      "text": "Okay, I'll note both of those. What about your medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 196.45,
      "end_seconds": 203.78,
      "duration_seconds": 7.33,
      "text": "Anxiety, for about a year. I've had an irregular heartbeat for two years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 204.81,
      "end_seconds": 205.76,
      "duration_seconds": 0.95,
      "text": "Mm, okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 207.18,
      "end_seconds": 226.14,
      "duration_seconds": 18.96,
      "text": "I've, I've had thin bones for five years now so, yes, high blood pressure it's the not knowing that gets to me i looked a few things up online, and that probably didn't help"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 227.21,
      "end_seconds": 234.4,
      "duration_seconds": 7.19,
      "text": "yes, an irregular heartbeat and thin bones are known to us, good to have that clear"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 243.52,
      "end_seconds": 245.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "Tell me your medicines, please."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 247.47,
      "end_seconds": 259.39,
      "duration_seconds": 11.92,
      "text": "I take escitalopram, 10 milligrams, once a day. Lisinopril i take it 10 milligrams, once a day. Peppermint capsules, after meals"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 260.61,
      "end_seconds": 262.31,
      "duration_seconds": 1.7,
      "text": "Who lives with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 263.7,
      "end_seconds": 266.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "My partner and our baby."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 266.97,
      "end_seconds": 269.46,
      "duration_seconds": 2.49,
      "text": "Have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 271.22,
      "end_seconds": 274.45,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "Erm, no, not at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 277.02,
      "end_seconds": 279.35,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "Let's move on to the examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 280.48,
      "end_seconds": 282.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "I'll listen to your chest now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 299.21,
      "end_seconds": 305.11,
      "duration_seconds": 5.9,
      "text": "your tummy is soft and not tender, and I can't feel any lumps"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 309.55,
      "end_seconds": 327.13,
      "duration_seconds": 17.58,
      "text": "that's all I needed to check so, based on the history and the examination, I think we're dealing with a functional bowel pattern, with no alarm features at this stage. Irritable bowel syndrome is still possible"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 328.34,
      "end_seconds": 332.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.96,
      "text": "uh, what are the odds it's serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 333.06,
      "end_seconds": 355.08,
      "duration_seconds": 22.02,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's a functional bowel pattern, with no alarm features, and we'll know more once the a coeliac blood test is back. a coeliac blood test is what I'd like next, for bloating. Try smaller meals and keep a food and symptom diary for four weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 355.31,
      "end_seconds": 364.32,
      "duration_seconds": 9.01,
      "text": "Mm, okay. Please take the tablets with food so they don't upset your stomach. I'd like you back in six weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 369.8,
      "end_seconds": 373.53,
      "duration_seconds": 3.73,
      "text": "Ah, um, good, I'll return then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 374.46,
      "end_seconds": 377.23,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "have I covered everything you wanted?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 378.78,
      "end_seconds": 383.42,
      "duration_seconds": 4.64,
      "text": "right, good, thanks, I'll see you then"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 385.47,
      "end_seconds": 386.91,
      "duration_seconds": 1.44,
      "text": "look after yourself"
    }
  ]
}